<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Free Aceh Movement</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1976–2005</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Gerakan Aceh Merdeka</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Free <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aceh">Aceh</a> Movement, Gerakan Aceh Merdeka, was a separatist organisation founded in 1976 by Hasan di Tiro to win independence for Aceh from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>. Its insurgency, met by heavy Indonesian military operations, cost thousands of lives. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-ocean">Indian Ocean</a> tsunami of 2004 devastated Aceh, peace talks led to the Helsinki agreement of August 2005, under which the movement disarmed and Aceh received special autonomy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/free-aceh-movement.jpg" alt="Free Aceh Movement" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Himasaram · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Free_Aceh_Movement.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
